  "interpretation": [
    "The resident exchanges perform no host upload or download inside their timed region; public exchanges include observation uploads and sample downloads.",
    "The 64-observation/32-sample medians are 0.373839 ms resident and 0.411191 ms public; the 1024-observation/256-sample medians are 4.712366 ms and 4.766709 ms.",
    "Eight-, sixteen- and twenty-bit grinding medians are 0.212391 ms, 0.341928 ms and 3.163219 ms. Twenty-bit samples span 0.344127 to 9.913518 ms because witness positions differ.",
    "Zero-bit grinding issues no GPU commands or transfers. Nonzero grinding downloads two public status words per candidate batch and performs no host upload."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This measures native CUDA transcript primitives with debug host orchestration, not an optimized complete prover or transaction throughput.",
    "Resident input uploads and final audit readback are outside the timed region, so resident/public latency differences are not an end-to-end proof speedup.",
    "No CPU performance baseline or OpenCL transcript timing is measured; CPU execution only supplies independent correctness audits.",
    "The small deterministic sample set is a checkpoint measurement, not a statistically broad production workload.",
    "Only the desktop RTX 5080 executes here; V100, laptop RTX 5080, Intel and AMD execution comparisons remain unmeasured."
  ],
